**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `RENAME_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingProxyTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests`
- `RENAME_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SeedingInMemoryTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests`

**How to implement.** The import seam moves into Domain under its new name (001 §B '`SeedingProxy` / `seedAll` become `CatalogueImport`'; .spec-md §3.4, §6 'Import seam'). This step moves and renames only: every behaviour, every fact's assertions (read through the new names) and the seed-fed `seedAll` stay as they are, and step 40 re-sources the orchestrator. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `module CatalogueImport` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `SampleStore.fs` (one `<Compile Include="CatalogueImport.fs" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no new comment). It holds the body of module `Seeding` (`OpticalConstructor.Seeding/Seeding.fs:30-130`) with these renames and no other change: `SeedingError` becomes `CatalogueImportError`, and its case `SeedRejectedErr` becomes `ImportRejectedErr`, still `of reason : string`; `SeedingProxy` becomes `CatalogueImportProxy`, still `[<ReferenceEquality>]`, with the four fields `saveCategory`, `saveMaterial`, `saveSample` and `saveLibraryEntry`, each answering `Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>`; and `InMemorySeedStores` becomes `InMemoryCatalogueStores` with its five fields. `seedAll` and `createInMemory` keep their names and bodies, and the file opens what `Seeding.fs` opens, except the namespace it now lives in. The module doc says in one to three lines that this is the library-import seam (spec 0050 §3.4). The 'DECLARED lifecycle' and 'later IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT' paragraphs (`Seeding.fs:10-29`) are dropped, not moved, because the lifecycle they describe has ended, and each member doc names the renamed types. (2) The `OpticalConstructor.Seeding` project is deleted: `Seeding.fs`, `OpticalConstructor.Seeding.fsproj` and the folder with its build output; its `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` entry (`:23-25`); and its one `ProjectReference`, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, with the comment above that reference. `git grep -n "OpticalConstructor.Seeding" -- "*.fsproj" "*.slnx"` lists no other. (3) Tests. `SeedingProxyTests.fs` becomes `CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs` (`module CatalogueImportProxyTests`) and `SeedingInMemoryTests.fs` becomes `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` (`module CatalogueImportInMemoryTests`), at the same compile positions. Each opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport` in place of `OpticalConstructor.Seeding.Seeding` and names the renamed types and case, and its module doc names `CatalogueImportProxy`. The two project-file comments above their old entries describe the retired seam and are deleted; none is added. Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, except that `a SeedingProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)` becomes `a CatalogueImportProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)`. (4) The doc comments that name the seam say `CatalogueImportProxy` and 'the catalogue import' instead, in no more words: `CategoryProxy.createInMemoryEmpty` in `MaterialLibrary.fs`, `MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty` in `MaterialStore.fs`, `SampleProxy.createInMemoryEmpty` in `SampleStore.fs` (`:189-191`), and `LibraryEntryStore` / `createInMemoryEmpty` in `ElementId.fs`.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `CatalogueImport.fs` MUST declare `CatalogueImportProxy` with exactly the fields `saveCategory`, `saveMaterial`, `saveSample` and `saveLibraryEntry`; the `OpticalConstructor.Seeding` folder and its `Berreman.slnx` entry MUST NOT exist; `git grep -n -E "SeedingProxy|OpticalConstructor.Seeding|SeedingError|SeedRejectedErr|InMemorySeedStores" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged, including the six renamed CatalogueImportProxyTests and CatalogueImportInMemoryTests facts; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.
